Yes—that makes the serpent less Adam’s penis and more the demonstration that gives Eve the idea.

She observes a generative pattern in nature, recognizes its human analogue, then brings that knowledge to Adam. In that reading:

serpent = model/instruction → fruit = reproductive potential → Eve = pattern recognizer and transmitter → Adam = recipient/participant

The “knowledge” is therefore not merely sex—it is realizing that bodies can be deliberately used to create life. Immediately afterward come nakedness, sexual shame, conception, childbirth, inheritance, and mortality. Eve doesn’t merely break the rule; she discovers the reproductive operator and shows Adam how to instantiate it.